  READ IT THIS WAY:
   · fill% near 100 means the basin is SATURATED — its people are capped by what
     the ground can feed, and raising capacity (irrigation) would raise them.
   · fill% well under 100 means the basin is still FILLING — capacity is not the
     binding constraint, and irrigation would hand it headroom it is not using.
   · a cradle whose org lags while its fill is low is held by the ORGANISATION
     machinery, not by its farmland, and irrigation would be a third correct-and-
     irrelevant lever.

